# Asset cache-bust on commit/push

When the user asks to **commit** and/or **push**, if the commit includes any client asset changes, bump the cache-bust version in the same commit.

## Treat as client asset changes

- `assets/css/**`
- `assets/js/**`
- `*.html` script/`link` tags that load local assets
- `site.webmanifest` (if linked with `?v=`)

Do **not** bump for backend-only changes (e.g. only `supabase/functions/**` or migrations) unless HTML/CSS/JS also change.

## How to bump

1. Set a new value in [`assets/asset-version.js`](assets/asset-version.js) (`SPLITIFY_ASSET_V`). Prefer a compact stamp like `YYYYMMDD` + a letter (`20261106d`).
2. Replace **every** matching `?v=...` with that same value in:
   - `bill.html`, `index.html`, `admin.html`
   - `@import` in `assets/css/style.css` (e.g. `brief-message.css?v=...`)
3. Keep all `?v=` values identical for a given ship; never leave mixed versions.

## Example

```javascript
// assets/asset-version.js
global.SPLITIFY_ASSET_V = '20261106d';
```

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/css/style.css?v=20261106d">
<script src="assets/js/pages/bill.js?v=20261106d"></script>
```
